{"_v":1,"id":"billy-elliot-the-musical-2008","cs":73,"rc":14,"bd":{"positive":10,"mixed":2,"negative":2},"rv":[{"cn":"Dominic Maxwell","o":"The Times (UK)","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/billy-elliot-review-this-revival-will-have-you-dancing-for-joy-zt63t2mwr"},{"cn":"Michael Kuchwara","o":"Associated Press","s":87,"b":"Rave","t":1,"q":"But 'Billy Elliot' is an exceptional work that exemplifies what the best musicals are all about: collaboration."},{"cn":"Linda Winer","o":"Newsday","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/710988585/","d":"2008-11-14","q":"\"Billy Elliot,\" the big, smart, London adaptation of the 2000 movie, finally arrived in a production as seriously thrilling as it is deeply lovable."},{"cn":"David Rooney","o":"Variety","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://variety.com/2008/legit/reviews/billy-elliot-the-musical-1200470924/","d":"2008-11-13","q":"That “Billy Elliot” is as much an elegy as a celebration is what makes it such a winner."},{"cn":"Charles McNulty","o":"Los Angeles Times","s":43,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.newspapers.com/image/193456095/","d":"2008-11-14","q":"(OK, provinces, cut the snickering.) In London, \"Billy Elliot\" managed to capitalize on its stirring saga to overcome Elton John's insipid pop-rock score and Lee Hall's clunky book and"},{"cn":"Terry Teachout","o":"The Wall Street Journal","s":29,"b":"Pan","t":1,"u":"https://online.wsj.com/article/SB122661564681526123.html#articleTabs%3Darticle","q":"If \"High School Musical\" didn't have the Disney brand plastered all over it, I doubt that very many people would bother to go see it, even in a production as pleasing as this one."},{"cn":"John Simon","o":"Bloomberg","s":87,"b":"Rave","t":2,"q":"Billy Elliot really does have something for everyone, and that something is, gloriously, art."},{"cn":"Joe Dziemianowicz","o":"New York Daily News","s":83,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.nydailynews.com/entertainment/arts/2008/11/14/2008-11-14_billy_elliot_makes_a_great_leap_onto_bro.html","d":"2008-11-14","q":"But even a few stumbles can't spoil a show that's so sweet and exhilarating that at times you feel like leaping."},{"cn":"Barbara Hoffman","o":"New York Post","s":83,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.nypost.com/p/entertainment/theater/item_gZiz25zzSc4NiWdUMdgVbL;jsessionid=FCBA306EC86346614244AA4FDEED36CA","q":"Granted, 'Billy Elliot' isn't perfect - a scene with giant dancing dresses might have gone AWOL from some Disney show on ice - but it's still head and toe-shoes above every other show this season. So thanks, Maggie Thatcher, for giving us something to sing about."},{"cn":"Thom Geier","o":"Entertainment Weekly","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"http://www.ew.com/ew/article/0,,20240252,00.html","q":"On the evidence so far, these young show-stoppers are nailing it."},{"cn":"Elysa Gardner","o":"USA Today","s":80,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.usatoday.com/life/theater/reviews/2008-11-13-billy-elliot_N.htm","d":"2008-11-13","q":"Those ideals — tolerance, empathy, individual expression — are noble ones, and director Stephen Daldry and his company infuse them with irresistible heart."},{"cn":"Michal Feingold","o":"Village Voice","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.villagevoice.com/2008-11-19/theater/faust-and-billy-elliot-souls-adrift-in-multimedia-saturn-returns-no-soul-at-all/","d":"2008-11-19","q":"The show's a mess, but it's a likable, good-hearted, overstuffed mess; you're more likely to go away feeling puzzled than feeling cheated by its unevenness."},{"cn":"Eric March","o":"Theater Life","s":100,"b":"Rave","t":3,"u":"https://theaterlife.com/billy-elliot/","d":"2011-09-18","q":"Billy Elliot the Musical is irresistible perfection."},{"cn":"Martin Denton","o":"Nytheatre","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"q":"The sequences where Billy learns to dance under the tutelage of Mrs. Wilkinson and her accompanist Mr. Braithwaite are gorgeous."}],"au":{"score":86,"designation":"